Third-party components
======================

Dependencies of the plugin (resolved with the plugin from the repositories of its build):

- commonmark-java 0.31.0 (org.commonmark:commonmark and the GFM tables, strikethrough,
  task list items and autolink extensions) - BSD 2-Clause License,
  https://github.com/commonmark/commonmark-java
- autolink-java 0.12.0 (org.nibor.autolink:autolink), used by the autolink extension -
  MIT License, https://github.com/robinst/autolink-java
- jsoup 1.23.2 (org.jsoup:jsoup) - MIT License, https://jsoup.org
- kotlinx.serialization 1.7.1 (org.jetbrains.kotlinx:kotlinx-serialization-json) -
  Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlinx.serialization
- Chicory 1.7.5 (com.dylibso.chicory:runtime, wasm), the WebAssembly runtime of rumdl -
  Apache License 2.0, https://github.com/dylibso/chicory

Contained in the plugin artifact, under io/github/wolfandrei/repodocs/:

- PlantUML 1.2026.9, the EPL build (net.sourceforge.plantuml:plantuml-epl), unmodified, as the
  file bundled/plantuml-epl-1.2026.9.jar - Eclipse Public License 2.0, https://plantuml.com.
  The jar contains third-party libraries under their own licenses, among them Guava (Apache
  License 2.0), Eclipse EMF and ELK (Eclipse Public License 2.0) and OpenPDF. The source code
  is the artifact net.sourceforge.plantuml:plantuml-epl:1.2026.9:sources on Maven Central and
  https://github.com/plantuml/plantuml. It runs in a separate JVM, not linked with the plugin.
- Xtend runtime 2.36.0 (org.eclipse.xtext:org.eclipse.xtext.xbase.lib), unmodified, as the file
  bundled/org.eclipse.xtext.xbase.lib-2.36.0.jar - Eclipse Public License 2.0,
  https://github.com/eclipse/xtext; the source code is its sources artifact on Maven Central.
- rumdl 0.3.4, the Markdown linter: the WebAssembly module of the npm package rumdl-wasm,
  compiled to JVM classes (lint/wasm/) - MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024-2025 Ruben J. Jongejan,
  https://github.com/rvben/rumdl; the license is the file bundled/rumdl-LICENSE.

Not part of the plugin, used when the project applies it:

- Dokka (org.jetbrains.dokka:dokka-gradle-plugin), the version of the project; the plugin
  compiles against its API and reads its HTML output - Apache License 2.0,
  https://github.com/Kotlin/dokka

The site does not use any network resources at run time: fonts are the system fonts of the
reader, and the scripts and styles of the site are part of this repository.
